    "title": "Good Friday 2026 stock market hours and closures",
    "text": "FINANCEIs the stock market open on Good Friday? Holiday schedules C. A. BridgesUSA TODAY NETWORK - FloridaApril 2, 2026, 9:53 a.m. ETOn Friday, April 3, Christians around the world observe Good Friday to commemorate the crucifixion of Jesus Christ, part of Holy Week that leads up to Easter Sunday. The day is observed with mourning, reflection, and special church services.Good Friday is not a federal holiday in the United States, but it is a state public holiday in Florida, and state offices and local courts may be closed. Some businesses and services may also be closed or have limited hours. Most banks will be open for regular business hours. Mail will be delivered as usual, as will UPS and FedEx services.",
